1
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:06,179
Need a quick GIF from a screen recording?

2
00:00:06,229 --> 00:00:10,109
Video to GIF Converter makes one right on
your desktop.

3
00:00:10,159 --> 00:00:14,160
FFmpeg is built in, so there is nothing
else to install.

4
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:18,049
Click Choose video, then pick your clip.

5
00:00:18,099 --> 00:00:20,540
This one is a short screen recording.

6
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:26,890
The app reads the video and shows its
size, frame rate, and length.

7
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:33,571
Set the frame rate to twelve, and the
width to four hundred eighty pixels.

8
00:00:33,621 --> 00:00:36,062
Lower numbers mean a smaller file.

9
00:00:36,112 --> 00:00:38,090
Loop forever is already on.

10
00:00:39,390 --> 00:00:43,263
Click Convert and save, and choose where
the GIF goes.

11
00:00:43,313 --> 00:00:45,879
A progress bar shows while it works.

12
00:00:45,929 --> 00:00:48,980
This short clip is done in about a second.

13
00:00:50,290 --> 00:00:55,327
When it finishes, the GIF plays right
inside the app, and you can see how big

14
00:00:55,377 --> 00:00:56,377
the file is.

15
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:00,590
Show in folder takes you straight to the
saved file.

16
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:05,146
Pick a video, choose two numbers, and get
a GIF.

17
00:01:05,196 --> 00:01:07,530
Everything stays on your computer.

